
EXERCISE 12: Packet Capture with Wireshark
Date: 31. Aug. 2026
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Aim: To study and use Wireshark to capture and analyse network packets.
Tools Required: Kali Linux, Wireshark, Metasploitable2.
Theory:
Wireshark is a network protocol analyser that captures and displays network traffic in real
time. It is used for:
 Troubleshooting network issues
 Analysing protocols
 Detecting suspicious traffic
 Learning network behaviour
Key Features:
 Live packet capture
 Display filters
 Protocol dissection
 Follow TCP/UDP streams
Procedure:
1. Start Wireshark:
sudo wireshark
2. Select interface (e.g., eth0).
3. Start capture.
4. Generate traffic:
ping 192.168.56.101
5. Apply display filters:
USC24301J, Basics of Ethical Hacking for Cyber Security
26
o icmp – Show only ICMP
o tcp.port == 80 – HTTP traffic
o ip.addr == 192.168.56.101 – Traffic to/from target
o http – HTTP requests/responses
6. Stop capture and analyse.
7. Save capture as .pcapng.
